From: FORZA-LAUNCHER-FOR-MAC-BLACKWELL-PROJECT
Subject: [PATCH] streaming: progress lines for a launcher (XODUS_PROGRESS=lines)

MetalHorizon 1.1.1. MetalHorizon runs `xodus-cli streaming` with its output going to a log file, where indicatif
draws nothing: the game's download showed only an indeterminate bar. With XODUS_PROGRESS=lines, the bars are hidden
and stdout gets `progress <bytes done> <bytes total>`: once when the files to fetch are known (done 0), at most twice
a second while they download, and once at the end (the run waits for that last line before it exits). Only the
files this run fetches count (the package's metadata, read before, does not): an update or a download started again
counts the files that differ from the last complete download. Without the variable nothing changes.

Applies to the tree MetalHorizon bundles xodus-cli from (work/xodus, app/build-app.sh XODUS_CLI_SRC) with patch -p1;
crates/xodus-cli/src/commands/streaming.rs is the same in work/xodus-ferestre, where it applies too.
Build: cargo build --release --offline -p xodus-cli. Tests: cargo test --release --offline -p xodus-cli streaming.
---
